    __be32 buf;
    ret = spi_read(data->spi, (void *) &buf, 3);
```
Reason:
The original code uses stack-allocated local variables (`__be16 buf` and `__be32 buf`) as buffers for `spi_read()`. Stack memory is not guaranteed to be DMA-safe; SPI transfers require buffers that are accessible by DMA to avoid data corruption or kernel crashes. Passing stack addresses to SPI functions violates the DMA-safe requirement.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
struct ti_adc_data {
	...
	u8 buf[3] __aligned(IIO_DMA_MINALIGN);
};
```
