    *val = get_unaligned_be16(data->buf);
```
```
case 3:
    ret = spi_read(data->spi, data->buf, 3);
    *val = get_unaligned_be24(data->buf);
```
Reason:
The fix adds a DMA-safe buffer (`data->buf`) inside the device structure, aligned to `IIO_DMA_MINALIGN` to ensure proper DMA access. Instead of using stack variables, `spi_read()` now uses this pre-allocated buffer. To correctly interpret the raw bytes, unaligned access helpers (`get_unaligned_be16` and `get_unaligned_be24`) are used, avoiding reliance on stack-based type casts that also violate alignment assumptions. This change ensures all SPI operations use DMA-safe memory.

